# Personal session context, not project rules. AGENTS.md is the committed,
# canonical file; CLAUDE.md holds credentials paths, working preferences and
# whatever is open this week, which is nobody else's business and stale within
# a fortnight. Same split as k8s-lookout.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# Built binaries. Every command here is `go run`, and the eval harnesses write
# their output under /tmp by default — so anything executable at the repo root
# is an absent-minded `go build` with no -o, and one of them is 40 MB.
/sre-agent
/sre-eval
/sre-eval-live
/sre-monitor

# Session scratch.
/resume

# Differential fingerprint vectors, generated by executing upstream's
# monitor_state.py. Deliberately not tracked: langchain-samples/sre-agent
# carries no licence, and output produced by running unlicensed code is the
# one artifact here that is genuinely derived from it rather than
# independently written. Regenerate locally with `go generate ./internal/monitor`
# — TestGoldenAgainstPython skips when the file is absent, so a fresh clone
# still passes, it just does not run that check. See dev/diffcheck.py.
/internal/monitor/testdata/golden.json
